<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n84140" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ποδ-ήρης</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ες</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>reaching to the feet,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πέπλοι, χιτὼν π.,</span> a robe <i>that
				falls over the feet,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Ba.</u>
				833
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Cyr.</u>
				6.4.2
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Paus.
				5.19.6
			</span></i>, etc. (later <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ποδήρης</span> alone
			(sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χιτών</span>) of the High Priest's
			robe, <i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>Ex.</u>
				25.6
			</span></i>, Aristeas<i><span class="en">
				96
			</span></i>); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. ἀσπίς</span> large shield
				<i>which covered the body down to the feet,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>An.</u>
				1.8.9
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Cyr.</u>
				6.2.10
			</span></i>: Com., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πώγων π. καθεῖται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					2.52c
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ναῦς π.</span> a ship <i>with feet,</i>
			i.e. <i>oars,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Eust.
				1515.29
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στῦλος π.</span> a <i>firmly
				based</i> pillar, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ag.</u>
				898
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ π.</span>
			<i>parts about the feet, feet,</i> ib.<i><span class="en">
				1594
			</span></i>. (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ήρης</span> perh. from <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ᾱρης,</span> cf. <i><span class="en">
				Arc.
			</span></i> pr. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ποδάρης.</span>)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
